{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793641941,"nonce":"2OQd3l/G3gYEYcb9DYy66w5cB2g=","title":"String + always copies; s += x in a loop is quadratic","message":"String + lowers to $IO$string_concat (ssa.rs), which allocates a new string and copies both operands. Python's s += x goes through combine_in_place (zyntax_python/src/lower.rs) with no accumulator or in-place append, although the SDK string has a BUILDER flag. TS and Lua concatenation share the lowering.\n\nRepro: s = ''; for i in range(100000): s += 'ab' takes about 400 ms (50,000 appends: 175 ms); CPython 4.5 ms. Same for s = s + x and while loops.\n\nDirection: when the left operand is a dead-after-use local, append in place into a builder with spare capacity.","files":null}]}